Dat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">findDeclarationRanges?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getModuleIdxFor?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">getD</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">modName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mods</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">mod</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">!</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rgs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">range</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">endPos</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pos</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reposToDat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">modName</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getRoot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reposToDat</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">msg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sorted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reposToDat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lengths</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"n\">toArray</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">qsort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">repo</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">repos</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zip</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sorted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">msg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">msg</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Data_toMessageData</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">repo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">threshold</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">joinSep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">msg</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toList</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 585909435,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776347733
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If produces a tally of all the declarations in the environment, split by provenance repo.</p>",
        "id": 585909578,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776347769
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Since the output is massive, it is foldable, which means that you will have to click a few times, starting from <code>Physlib</code> and then on <code>x more entries</code>, until you get to the longest ones.</p>",
        "id": 585909848,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776347831
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If there are at most <code>3</code> declarations with the same length, then you can expand the appropriate tab and see what the declarations are.  The number <code>3</code> is the <code>threshold</code> parameter in the <code>run_cmd</code> that you can modify.</p>",
        "id": 585910155,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776347903
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The reason for not printing everything out by default is that it would overflow the infoview.</p>",
        "id": 585910263,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776347929
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>length 129: decls 1<br>\n<code>Electromagnetism.ElectromagneticPotential.kineticTerm_add_time_mul_const</code></p>\n<p>length 131: decls 2<br>\n<code>SuperSymmetry.SU5.ChargeSpectrum.allowsTermQ10_or_allowsTerm_of_allowsTerm_insertQ10</code> <code>Space.IsDistBounded.integrable_mul_inv_pow</code></p>\n<p>length 132: decls 1<br>\n<code>FieldSpecification.WickAlgebra.bosonicProjF_mem_ideal</code></p>\n<p>length 136: decls 1<br>\n<code>WickContraction.signFinset_insertAndContract_some</code></p>\n<p>length 142: decls 1<br>\n<code>FieldSpecification.WickAlgebra.ι_timeOrderF_superCommuteF_eq_time</code></p>\n<p>length 147: decls 2<br>\n<code>Physlib.Fin.involutionCons Space.distDiv_inv_pow_eq_dim</code></p>\n<p>length 150: decls 1<br>\n<code>Electromagnetism.ElectromagneticPotential.time_deriv_time_deriv_electricField_of_isExtrema</code></p>\n<p>length 155: decls 1<br>\n<code>Space.time_integral_hasFDerivAt</code></p>\n<p>length 158: decls 1<br>\n<code>HasVarAdjoint.adjFDeriv_apply</code></p>\n<p>length 163: decls 1<br>\n<code>QuantumMechanics.OneDimension.HarmonicOscillator.orthogonal_exp_of_mem_orthogonal</code></p>\n<p>length 179: decls 1<br>\n<code>ClassicalMechanics.HarmonicOscillator.InitialConditions.trajectories_unique</code></p>\n<p>length 215: decls 1<br>\n<code>fundamental_theorem_of_variational_calculus'</code></p>",
        "id": 585911024,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776348084
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"653351\">Joseph Tooby-Smith</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/479953-Physlib/topic/Technical.20debt/near/585806501\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(I would also like to add a counter for 'long proofs' (by line length), but all the above where done with a bash script, and I think this would only be possible with a lean script)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Mathlib has a linter that flags empty lines in commands (and I think that it ignores empty lines in docstrings and module docs).  If Physlib has that linter active, then a bash script can be pretty accurate in determining data like the above, with minimal false positives/negatives.</p>",
        "id": 585911868,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776348252
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is amazing, thank you <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"321459\">@Damiano Testa</span>. We don't have this linter turned on (though we should), but we do have other checks in about empty lines.</p>",
        "id": 585919939,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Tooby-Smith",
        "timestamp": 1776350019
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The actual list is interesting! Has somethings I wouldn't naively expect.</p>",
        "id": 585920115,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Tooby-Smith",
        "timestamp": 1776350061
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The linter suggestion is just to get more \"regex-like\" searches to be closer to being correct.  For Physlib, it probably could make sense to enforce it.  For programming projects, I think that it would be mostly noise, since formatting a program (instead of a proof) has quite a bit of value.</p>",
        "id": 585920325,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776350103
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe worth exploring if we could use this: <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113486\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113486-General-announcements/topic/Scanning.20Mathlib.20with.20Shouyi.3A.20A.20Human-in-the-Loop.20Maintenanc/with/593001959\">#General announcements &gt; Scanning Mathlib with Shouyi: A Human-in-the-Loop Maintenanc</a>  here</p>",
        "id": 593003592,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Tooby-Smith",
        "timestamp": 1777987156
    }
]